WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.887
Three documents.

00:00:02.967 --> 00:00:04.791
Each one looks anonymous.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.161
But put them side by side,

00:00:06.241 --> 00:00:09.205
and they point to just one person.

00:00:12.103 --> 00:00:13.683
This is Mosaic.

00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:15.332
It catches what you never realized you

00:00:15.412 --> 00:00:17.447
were revealing.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.314
Redaction tools hunt for names and emails.

00:00:22.394 --> 00:00:24.357
Mosaic checks how your next draft combines

00:00:24.437 --> 00:00:27.269
with everything you’ve already published.

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:30.009
Your private documents never leave your browser.

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:32.319
The cloud only writes generic test packs,

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.258
from a fixed list of categories,

00:00:34.338 --> 00:00:38.266
and only after you approve the exact request.

00:00:38.661 --> 00:00:39.916
Open a workspace,

00:00:39.996 --> 00:00:42.052
hit review, and Mosaic lights up the

00:00:42.132 --> 00:00:43.155
passages that matter,

00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:46.534
with evidence from every release side by side.

00:00:46.614 --> 00:00:48.902
Every result says where it ran.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.096
With no built-in model on this machine,

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:55.150
the sample shows clearly labelled sample results.

00:00:55.382 --> 00:00:57.345
The disclosure map shows exactly how the

00:00:57.425 --> 00:00:59.842
draft connects to earlier releases.

00:00:59.922 --> 00:01:01.328
In this fictional sample,

00:01:01.408 --> 00:01:03.487
three small details narrow a hundred people

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.463
down to one.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:09.009
Mosaic suggests safer wording that keeps your point.

00:01:09.089 --> 00:01:10.437
Apply it, review again,

00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:14.165
and that group grows from one to twenty-one.

00:01:14.562 --> 00:01:15.922
Need new tests?

00:01:16.002 --> 00:01:17.884
You see the exact request before anything

00:01:17.964 --> 00:01:19.207
leaves your device.

00:01:19.287 --> 00:01:20.403
Just categories.

00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:21.529
No text.

00:01:21.609 --> 00:01:23.668
No names.

00:01:23.907 --> 00:01:24.953
While building Mosaic,

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:26.544
we found a real gap.

00:01:26.624 --> 00:01:28.517
In browsers without the built-in model,

00:01:28.597 --> 00:01:32.000
the SDK’s on-device-only mode quietly sends requests

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.266
to the cloud.

00:01:33.346 --> 00:01:35.298
Mosaic’s guard blocks that.

00:01:35.378 --> 00:01:38.539
Zero private requests got through.

00:01:39.644 --> 00:01:41.735
Got a scan or a photo?

00:01:41.815 --> 00:01:43.999
Mosaic reads it with OCR,

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:44.974
right on your device,

00:01:45.054 --> 00:01:48.564
and flags any words it isn’t sure about.

00:01:48.989 --> 00:01:50.767
Approve the release on your device,

00:01:50.847 --> 00:01:51.997
export a clean copy,

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:54.318
and you’re done.

00:01:54.398 --> 00:01:55.572
And it feels right at home on

00:01:55.652 --> 00:01:57.466
your phone.

00:01:58.333 --> 00:02:00.113
It’s measured, too.

00:02:00.307 --> 00:02:01.968
On our open synthetic benchmark,

00:02:02.048 --> 00:02:04.139
the rules baseline alone scores one hundred

00:02:04.219 --> 00:02:07.648
percent precision and forty-four percent recall.

00:02:07.842 --> 00:02:10.782
On-device model runs are next.

00:02:12.103 --> 00:02:13.172
Mosaic.

00:02:13.252 --> 00:02:15.134
Protect the information you never realized you

00:02:15.214 --> 00:02:16.121
were revealing.

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:17.865
Try it free today.
